From: Pocket EVO integration <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: pwm-fan: drop sleep supply after EVO charging policy

Adapt source b367e5c after 9071, preserving charging-on behavior and
restoring awake PWM on suspend failure. Also cut supply when charging mode
is configured but external power is absent.

--- a/drivers/hwmon/pwm-fan.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/pwm-fan.c
@@ -577,6 +577,8 @@
 
 	ctx->charging_valid = false;
 	ret = on ? __set_pwm(ctx, ctx->pwm_sleep_charging) : pwm_fan_power_off(ctx, true);
+	if (!ret && !on)
+		ret = pwm_fan_switch_power(ctx, false);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_warn(ctx->dev, "failed to turn the fan %s in sleep: %d\n", on ? "on" : "off", ret);
 		return ret;
@@ -869,6 +871,10 @@
 		}
 	} else {
 		ret = pwm_fan_power_off(ctx, true);
+		if (!ret)
+			ret = pwm_fan_switch_power(ctx, false);
+		if (ret)
+			__set_pwm(ctx, ctx->pwm_awake);
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&ctx->lock);
 
